 "intro": "Hatra in the Mesopotamian desert, 199 AD. The city beat Trajan in 117. You are Septimius Severus, just back from sacking Ctesiphon.",
 "debrief": "In Cassius Dio’s account, Severus besieged Hatra twice. The defenders burned his engines with naphtha and threw pots of stinging insects at the attackers. When a breach was made, Severus called off the attack, expecting the city to surrender to save its temple treasures; the walls were rebuilt overnight. His European troops then refused to attack, and the Syrians who did were cut down. After twenty days he gave up. The other choices are what-ifs.",
